    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 11 slate with **Yordan Alvarez** standing as our premier offensive anchor. Posting an elite score of 76.54, **Yordan Alvarez** faces a favorable matchup against Rocker, buoyed by a robust 0.469 xwOBA and an optimal #2 spot in the lineup. Close behind is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.81), whose value is significantly elevated by his lead-off role and a strong 4.76 xERA matchup against Lodolo. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** faces a dynamic platoon disadvantage that suppresses his base projection by 15%, his projected opportunity to impact the stolen base category makes him a high-leverage start, assuming he maintains the leadoff spot in the official lineup.\n\nPlatoon edges are driving several mid-tier starts today. **Lars Nootbaar** (55.37) and **Christian Yelich** (54.65) benefit from favorable L/R splits despite park factors being slightly restrictive. Notably, **Trea Turner** remains a high-floor play (58.63) despite a tough matchup against Mize; while his speed is stifled by the pitcher's elite hold rate, his presence at the top of the order remains indispensable for our scoring targets. Among our bench options, **Casey Schmitt** came closest to cracking the lineup with a 45.79 score. Ultimately, **Casey Schmitt** was relegated to the pine because his platoon disadvantage against the lefty Freeland lowered his efficiency below the established threshold, and our roster depth preferred the higher ceiling of players like **Kyle Schwarber** (57.99) against Mize.\n\nWe are monitoring significant weather risks for today\u2019s contest. **Gary Sanchez**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** all carry rain risk flags between 31% and 45%, which could lead to condensed plate appearances or sudden scoring shifts. Owners should exercise caution with **Gary Sanchez** and **Caleb Durbin**, as the high probability of rain, combined with their reliance on specific lineup placements, introduces volatility into their respective efficiency scores. We continue to hold **Hyeseong Kim** in the minors, awaiting his return to the active roster to bolster our middle infield depth.",
